\citation{Knop2009}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The upwind-frequency choice on CMFGEN's frequency grid (sweeping high $\rightarrow $ low $\nu $). In expanding gas ($\Gamma > 0$) photons redshift, so the photons at the current point came from the \emph  {previous}, higher frequency, already computed. In a compression zone ($\Gamma < 0$) photons blueshift: they came from the \emph  {next}, lower frequency, not yet computed in this sweep. The Knop solver uses it anyway, from the previous \emph  {iteration}'s stored values.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:upwind}{{2}{4}{The upwind-frequency choice on CMFGEN's frequency grid (sweeping high $\rightarrow $ low $\nu $). In expanding gas ($\Gamma > 0$) photons redshift, so the photons at the current point came from the \emph {previous}, higher frequency, already computed. In a compression zone ($\Gamma < 0$) photons blueshift: they came from the \emph {next}, lower frequency, not yet computed in this sweep. The Knop solver uses it anyway, from the previous \emph {iteration}'s stored values}{figure.2}{}}
