\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The two formal solvers side by side. Left: the original path, which implicitly requires $\Gamma >0$ (monotonic expansion) and fails in compression zones. Right: the Knop et al.\ (2009) path: the opacity carries only $|\Gamma |$, the signed coupling $Q$ lives in the source function, the upwind neighbour is chosen by the sign of $\Gamma $, and the not-yet-computed $I_{\rm  NEXT}$ is supplied from the previous great iteration.}}{6}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:flowchart}{{3}{6}{The two formal solvers side by side. Left: the original path, which implicitly requires $\Gamma >0$ (monotonic expansion) and fails in compression zones. Right: the Knop et al.\ (2009) path: the opacity carries only $|\Gamma |$, the signed coupling $Q$ lives in the source function, the upwind neighbour is chosen by the sign of $\Gamma $, and the not-yet-computed $I_{\rm NEXT}$ is supplied from the previous great iteration}{figure.3}{}}
